  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read proxy.admission_currency_gate (the nine admission_enforcer files have no diff) and proxy.admission_gate_unskippable (pre_admission/standing.rs: the TransportBindingChecked event is now written at each return instead of bound to a local first; same event, same arms). The cited serving tests in mcp-re-proxy/tests/integration_async/admission_currency_serving_test.rs were split into fixtures, outage, rig and wire modules. I compared the twelve cited tests with their old bodies and read the helpers they now call: Rig::new builds the same delegated proxy (same resolver, replay tier, counting inner, signer and with_admission arguments as the old replica function), confirm_live signs admission_claims(5, Admitted, NOW - 30) and serves at NOW, serve_claims and serve_bare sign with the authority key or with no evidence over the same request, assert_refused checks 403, the admission-refused wire code and the backend call count, and the store-writer test builds the same forged state record over u64::MAX with another key. Every status, wire code, backend call count and facet expectation is the same. Dependency THM-0005 is REVIEWED. The claim holds. The mutation lane was not run, and no test was run. Evidence class as registered (V0).",
